## Score a frozen example in AppKernel JS

Unlock the named Key Vault entry selected in AI grader settings and enable the grader. With a saved training example and the exact text of the rubric revision under test, run

```js
const { accepted, acceptProbability, model, requestId, rubricVersion } =
  await suggestionGrader.gradeExample({
    base: example.base,
    diff: example.diff,
    rubric: { version: rubricRevisionId, instructions: frozenRubricMarkdown }
  })
```

The call replays the self-contained records and sends only normalized cell content and operations. It uses the supplied rubric text verbatim. The caller supplies and records the version identifier. The grader returns the probability attached to the `accept` choice even when `reject` wins. A missing probability raises an error. The request ID comes from the response header and can be null if the service does not expose it.
